 "title": "Two Communication Skills to Get Ahead",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator claims that to become a better communicator and make people want to listen, you must master two skills: fluency and coherence. Fluency means speaking a language comfortably without struggling for words, while coherence means speaking clearly, efficiently, and to the point.",
 "key_points": [
  "Master fluency and coherence to go from not being able to express thoughts to being a clear speaker.",
  "Fluency means being able to speak the English language so comfortably that you do not struggle to find the right words and sentences.",
  "Good English alone is not enough if you speak in circles or take one hour to say what can be said in 10 minutes.",
  "Along with fluency, you need to speak clearly in a way that makes sense and be as efficient as possible with your words and sentences.",
  "Speaking to the point is when people will listen to you until the end and take your ideas seriously."
 ],
 "content": "These 2 skills can put you ahead of 89% of professionals. How To Explain Sh*t? What You Say: Understand, Outcome, Fastest Way, Anticipate Questions. How You Say: Top down, Storytelling, Energy, Cadence. Let's make you a better communicator. If you want to go from being a person who's not able to express their thoughts properly to becoming a person who speaks so clearly, people would actually crave to listen to you, just master these two skills: fluency and coherence. What is the meaning of this? Fluency means being able to speak the English language so comfortably, you don't have to struggle to find the right words and sentences, just like how you speak your native language, which is not enough. Now you tell me, if my English is good, but I keep going in circles, would you listen to me? The answer is no. My English is good, but what I speak is useless, would you listen to me? The answer is no. My English is good, but I take one hour to say what can be said in just 10 minutes, would you listen to me? The answer is no. That is why along with fluency, you also need to speak clearly, in a way that actually makes sense, and learn to be as efficient as possible with your words and sentences, so you speak to the point. That is when people will listen to you till the end and take your ideas seriously. Comment “SPEAK” to get your communication audited.",
